  "details": "PHP is an HTML-embedded scripting language commonly used with the Apache HTTP Server.  \n\nSecurity Fix(es):  \n\n  * php: ext-pgsql: PHP: SQL injection via improper backslash escaping (CVE-2026-17543)\n  * php: PHP: Denial of Service via circular symbolic links in phar archives (CVE-2026-7260)\n\n\nBug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):  \n\n  * Rebase PHP to 8.3.33 for CVE-2026-17543 and CVE-2026-7260 in 10.2.z (JIRA:AlmaLinux-223946)\n\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.\n",
